# Auto Memory

This file is Claude's tactical memory — auto-written observations, patterns, and feedback that accumulate across sessions. Claude maintains it; you read it; both of you reference it.

## How this differs from CLAUDE.md

| | CLAUDE.md | MEMORY.md (this file) |
|---|---|---|
| **Who writes it** | You (curated) | Claude (auto-observations) |
| **Pace of change** | Slow, intentional | Fast, organic |
| **Content** | Strategic instructions | Tactical observations |
| **Length goal** | Under 500 lines | Index of topic files |
| **First load** | Every session | First 200 lines auto-loaded |

## Topic Files (read on demand)

Memory is organized as small topic files in this directory. This index has one line per topic. Read individual files when their topic comes up.

[Add lines as memory accumulates. Format: `- topic_name.md — one-line hook`]

Example entries (delete these once you have real ones):

- `feedback_communication_style.md` — How user prefers updates phrased; tone calibration.
- `pattern_session_end_routine.md` — User's habit of running /kit:reflect → /kit:session-end at close.
- `project_active_work.md` — What's currently in flight; updated at session end.
- `tool_quirks.md` — Known issues with tools/MCP servers; workarounds.

## Tags

When writing memory entries, use these tags for pattern detection:

- `[PATTERN]` — Recurring behavior or preference (positive or negative)
- `[DRIFT]` — Moment Claude drifted from partnership principles
- `[FRICTION]` — Something that slowed work or caused unnecessary effort
- `[TOOL-GAP]` — Missing tool or capability that would have helped
- `[DEAD-END]` — Approach that failed (also log to ~/.claude/dead-ends.md)
- `[CONTEXT-GAP]` — Missing information that caused problems
- `[WIN]` — Something that worked exceptionally well

## Maintenance

Twice a month or so:
- Review topic files. Delete what's no longer true.
- Promote stable patterns from MEMORY.md → CLAUDE.md (curated rules)
- Demote outdated CLAUDE.md rules → MEMORY.md (with sunset date)
- Keep this index under ~50 lines. If it's longer, consolidate adjacent topics.

> WARNING: Files larger than ~200 lines or 30KB get partially loaded. Keep index entries to one line and move detail into topic files.
